    "lawCode": "Add §404-ff, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S287\n\nSPONSOR: RHOADS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to establishing\na distinctive plate honoring Eagle Scouts\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAmends the Vehicle and Traffic Law to allow for distinctive plates for\nEagle Scouts\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection l.the vehicle and traffic Law is amended by adding a new section\n404-ff\n\nSubdivision 1, any person residing within New York State, upon request,\nbe issued a distinctive plate in support of the Eagle Scouts.\n\nSubdivision 2, an application for such plate be filed with the commis-\nsioner as commissioner shall prescribe.\n\nSubdivision 3, Establishes that the plate will be issued in the same\nmanner as other numbered license plates upon the payment of the regular\nregistration fee and an initial one time service charge of twenty-five\ndollars.\n\nSection 2. states that a distinctive plate can only be designed,\nproduced and issued upon the delivery to the department of a surety bond\nin the amount of six thousand dollars. However if the Commissioner\nreceives prior to the plate design at least two hundred orders with the\nannual service charge, no such surety bond will be required.\n\nSubdivision 2, deems that if upon the expiration of two years following\nthe date upon which distinctive plates in the series are first available\nfor sale two hundred or more sets of such plates are sold, a bond would\nbe discontinued. If fewer than two hundred sets are sold, the department\nwould be enti- tled to recover against the bond in an amount propor-\ntionate to such shortfall.\n\nSection 3 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, The State of New York makes available many different distinc-\ntive license plates to members of various groups. As such, this legis-\nlation would make it possible for Eagle Scouts to display the accom-\nplishment of many years of dedication to complete the seven different\nranks culminating with being awarded the rank of Eagle Scout.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
